        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): chat workspace panel leaves an empty gap when collapsed",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where collapsing the session workspace panel in the Control UI chat view still reserved a 52px empty rail on the right edge. The chat content stopped short of the window, leaving a permanent dead gap with two orphaned icons floating in it — the panel looked half-closed instead of closed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen the workspace rail is collapsed, the workbench grid now drops the rail column entirely (`minmax(0, 1fr)` single column) and the expand toggle floats over the chat's top-right corner as a small glass button, matching the existing circular nav-toggle pattern. The decorative file icon in the collapsed strip was removed along with its now-dead CSS; the expanded rail is unchanged. The toggle keeps its accessible name (`Expand session workspace`) and `aria-expanded` state.\n\n## User Impact\n\nClosing the workspace panel now gives the full width back to the chat. The expand control stays visible and clickable in the top-right corner, so the panel remains one click away.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Before** — collapsed panel still reserves an empty rail (note the gap on the right edge):\n\n![before: collapsed rail reserves an empty 52px column](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/workspace-rail-collapse/before-collapsed.png)\n\n**After** — collapsed panel frees the full width; the expand toggle floats in the corner:\n\n![after: collapsed rail takes no width, floating expand toggle](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/workspace-rail-collapse/after-collapsed.png)\n\n**After (expanded)** — the open panel is unchanged:\n\n![after: expanded workspace rail unchanged](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/workspace-rail-collapse/after-expanded.png)\n\nValidation:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/ui/views/chat.test.ts` — 137 passed, including the updated collapsed-rail test asserting the workbench drops the rail column and the floating toggle stays reachable.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/ui/e2e/chat-flow.e2e.test.ts` — 19 passed (Playwright), covering collapse → expand → collapse round-trips and the ≤1120px viewport where the rail hides entirely.\n- Screenshots captured with the repo's Playwright e2e harness (mock gateway, light theme, 1360×860@2x) on this branch; \"before\" captured from the parent commit with the same harness.\n- `oxfmt --check` and `scripts/run-oxlint.mjs` clean on touched files.\n",
